TI  - AN INVESTIGATION OF MEDIATORS FOR THE RELATIONSHIP BETWEEN PARENT MENTAL HEALTH AND ADOLESCENT PROBLEMATIC INTERNET USE: A CROSS-SECTIONAL STUDY IN ROMANIAN ADOLESCENTS
T2  - JOURNAL OF EVIDENCE-BASED PSYCHOTHERAPIES
AB  - Problematic Internet use (PIU) in adolescents is associated with parental mental health. However, no study investigated mechanisms which can explain this relationship. Therefore, the aim of the present study was to investigate parental PIU, parenting dimensions and adolescent mental health as significant mediators of the relationship between parental mental health and adolescent PIU. Two-hundred-twenty-two parents (M-age = 41.36; SD = 3.05) and adolescents (M-age = 15.91; SD = .95) participated in this cross-sectional study. Results indicated significant associations between parental mental health, namely parental social anxiety symptoms and parental depressive symptoms, parental PIU, positive parenting, adolescent emotional problems and adolescent PIU. Multiple mediation analysis indicated that parental PIU, positive parenting and adolescent emotional problems were significant mediators in the relationship between parental mental health and adolescent PIU. Implications for prevention and intervention programs for PIU involving both adolescents and their parents are discussed.
